From 9b129fba7f1d133ebdc15b3eb260fbd074a13eb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 744474391 <744474391@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 08:11:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add asym wf3 firmware (4 RX + 3 WF, ch0 = 16K FFT) and 125
 MHz CIC fix

*** RaspSDR 125 MHz hardware ONLY -- do NOT use on 66.666 MHz KiwiSDR ***

== New bitstream: RaspSDR.rx4.wf3.bit (FPGA_ID = 5, fw_sel = 4) ==
- 4 audio receivers: identical audio path/buffers/12 kHz rate as rx4.wf4
- 3 waterfall channels:
    ch0: 16384-deep sample buffer / 16384-point FFT
    ch1, ch2: unchanged 8192/8192
- RTL gated by `ifdef USE_WF_ASYM16K; the wf4/wf2/wf3/wf0 builds are
  byte-for-byte unchanged when the define is absent
- new ipcore_bram_16k_32b (14 RAMB36) + iq_sampler_16k_32b (14-bit addrs)
- waterfall_1cic gains a SAMPLER_16K parameter (generate-if 8K/16K sampler)
- receiver.v splits WF instances: ch0 single (16K) + ch1..2 array (8K)
- make_proj.tcl: --rx4_wf3_asym switch, output RaspSDR.rx4.wf3.bit
- host C: fw_sel=4 branch, wf_chan_nsamps() returns 16384 only for
  asym ch0 (8192 on every other config/path)

== 125 MHz CIC correction ==
The shipped kiwi.config had the 66.666 MHz decimation values active on a
125 MHz RaspSDR, worked around in software by "rx_decim *= 2" (a -6.2%
rate hack). Corrected to the real 125 MHz coefficients:
- RX1_STD_DECIM 505/11 -> 947/11
- RX1_WIDE_DECIM 823/4 -> 1543/4
- removed the "if (raspsdr) rx_decim *= 2" hack in main.cpp
- regenerated kiwi.gen.vh and cic_rx1_12k/20k.vh
  (RX_DECIM_4CH = 10417, 125 MHz / 10417 = 11999.6 Hz)
WF CIC coefficients (R=8192) are unchanged.

== Versioning ==
- VERSION_SUFFIX "-wf3-asym": startup banner shows
  "KiwiSDR v1.583-wf3-asym [mod: BH4RRG]"
- version_suffix added to web MSG / config_cb JSON; kiwi.js status bar
  renders "v1.583-wf3-asym"; base version stays v1.583
- kiwi.min.js/kiwisdr.min.js rebuilt unminified (no JS minifier on the
  build host; ~15 KB larger gzipped)

mod: BH4RRG
